  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for reliability and a willingness to learn. They judge you by honesty, progress and the skills you show.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is keeping a weekly study log you actually follow.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and backlogs and failed degree subjects: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools explain topics and generate practice questions. Routine revision aids are easy to get.
  </p>
  <p>
    Steady effort, honesty and the habit of fixing gaps hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explain and quiz; later, own your results.
  </p>

